CORE
main.c
module.c --dump-c
^\s*union \{ struct A\$0 \*p; \} u;$
^\s*union \{ struct A \*p; \} u;$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^\s*union anonymous.* u;$
^warning: ignoring
--
Linking renames the struct types of one of the files, including an anonymous
union (see regression/cbmc/Linking10). The union must remain recognisable as
anonymous for dump-c to emit the member u of either struct S with an inline
union type rather than with a named one.
